WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
If your prep is PEG, this video will walk you through exactly how to take it,

2
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.260
just follow along step by step.

3
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.540
Your PEG prep is the large container that you'll mix with water.

4
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.750
You'll also want Crystal Light or flavor packs on hand if you'd like to improve

5
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:14.540
the taste.

6
00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.240
At 8 a.m. the day before your procedure, you'll mix the prep.

7
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.410
Add water to your prep container and stir or shake until everything is fully

8
00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:23.280
dissolved.

9
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.840
Once it's mixed, put it in the refrigerator.

10
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.560
Keeping it cold makes it much easier to drink.

11
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.480
If you're adding Crystal Light or a flavor pack, you can mix that in now.

12
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.960
Just make sure it's not red, orange, blue, or purple.

13
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.640
Stick to clear or light-colored flavors.

14
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.120
Between 4 and 5 p.m. you'll begin drinking the solution.

15
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.440
Here's the pace.

16
00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:48.600
Drink 16 ounces, that's about two cups, every 30 minutes.

17
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.630
You'll keep going at that pace for about 4 hours until the entire container

18
00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:53.200
is empty.

19
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.680
Take your time with each glass.

20
00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:01.020
Slow, steady sips are easier on your stomach than trying to gulp it all at once

21
00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:01.280
.

22
00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.880
This part is really important.

23
00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.670
You must drink all of the prep solution as directed, even if you're already

24
00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.120
passing

25
00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.120
clear liquid.

26
00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:12.570
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

27
00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:13.360
the clearest

28
00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.080
view during your procedure.

29
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.600
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule, and neither

30
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:20.760
of

31
00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:26.360
us wants that, once you've finished, keep drinking clear liquids until bedtime.

32
00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:31.280
Staying hydrated will help you feel better and help the prep do its job.

33
00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.000
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom, applying

34
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:35.920
a petroleum-based

35
00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:39.160
ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

36
00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.160
That's it.

37
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:41.160
You've got this.

38
00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:45.080
Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay hydrated.

39
00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:48.440
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office.

40
00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:49.500
We're here to help.
